# calendar-overview — .env template (NO REAL SECRETS — safe to commit)
# Copy to ~/.hermes/.env and fill in values:
#
# REQUIRED:
#   MSFT_CLIENT_ID — Application (client) ID from Microsoft Entra app registration.
#   This is the SAME id as your morning-digest app — no new app registration
#   is needed. Calendars.Read is already a delegated scope for that app.
#   Get one: see after-install.md or docs/entra-registration-guide.md.
#
# OPTIONAL (do not set unless you know why):
#   MSFT_AUTHORITY     — override the default "organizations" (e.g. "common", tenant guid)
#   MSFT_REDIRECT_URI  — override the default loopback "http://127.0.0.1:8765/callback"
#   MSFT_UPN           — user principal name/email (used for @me detection + self-match)
#
# Populated after the `login`/`consume` steps — DO NOT commit these real values:
#   MSFT_ACCESS_TOKEN=***
#   MSFT_REFRESH_TOKEN=***
#   MSFT_TOKEN_EXPIRES_AT=***
#
# Memory search reads $OBSIDIAN_VAULT_PATH for agenda/@ pointers (offline grep):
#   OBSIDIAN_VAULT_PATH=/home/pele/notes   # resolved, no secret
#
# NOTE: MSFT_CLIENT_ID is a public identifier (not a secret) — safe in .env.example.
#       MSFT_ACCESS_TOKEN / MSFT_REFRESH_TOKEN are per-user secrets — keep in .env only.
